  "translationRepairs": [
    ["s0003","idiomatic","(Auspicious Ceremonies, Part One)〉","(Auspicious Ceremonies, Part One)","s0003 Chinese 〈（嘉儀上）〉 is rendered with English parentheses; the trailing book-title closer 〉 in the idiomatic field is stray markup with no English opener, and removing it leaves an accurate section title.","high","applied"],
    ["s0003","literal","(Auspicious Ceremonies, Part One)〉","(Auspicious Ceremonies, Part One)","Same stray 〉 appears in the literal field for 〈（嘉儀上）〉; stripping the unmatched closer yields the correct English section title without inventing or omitting meaning.","high","applied"],
    ["s0120","idiomatic","The Palace Commissioner calls for the emperor to bow twice and proclaim, \"Long live the Emperor!\"; the assembled ministers in attendance bow.","The Commissioner of the Palace Secretariat calls for the emperor to bow twice and proclaim, \"Long live the Emperor!\"; the assembled ministers in attendance bow.","s0120 has 宣徽使, already rendered “Commissioner of the Palace Secretariat” in adjacent s0118 and in this unit’s literal; “Palace Commissioner” is an inconsistent, vaguer mistranslation of the same office, and the proposed title restores consistency without changing the action.","high","applied"],
    ["s0224","literal","The empress takes leave of her parents, paternal uncles and aunts, and elder brothers, each bowing four times;","The empress takes leave of her parents, paternal uncles and aunts, and elder brothers, bowing four times to each;","後辭父母、伯叔父母、兄，各四拜 has the empress as subject taking leave, with 各四拜 meaning she bows four times to each relative; “each bowing four times” wrongly makes the relatives the agents, and the proposed wording matches the Chinese and the idiomatic field.","high","applied"],
    ["s0233","literal","She is borne with a silver pitcher on her back, silk bands in hand, and walks the yellow path.","Bearing a silver pitcher on her back and silk bands in her hands, she walks the yellow path.","負銀罌，捧縢，履黃道行 uses active 負 “bear on the back” and 捧 “hold”; “is borne with” invents a passive carrying absent from the Chinese, and the proposed active wording restores the correct agent.","high","applied"],
    ["s0242","literal","The empress's elder and younger sisters or younger sisters, and those who accompanied her in bowing, each receive gifts.","The empress's elder or younger sisters, and those who accompanied her in bowing, each receive gifts.","後姊若妹 uses 若 as “or” (elder or younger sisters); the literal’s “elder and younger sisters or younger sisters” duplicates 妹 and garbles the connective, and “elder or younger sisters” is the accurate fix.","high","applied"],
    ["s0247","idiomatic","they bow once more, advance slightly, and submit on behalf the words of those who escorted the empress;","they bow once more, advance slightly, and submit the words of those who escorted the empress;","“submit on behalf the words” is ungrammatical, but inserting “their” still yields awkward English with an unclear antecedent; 附奏送後之詞 means they present the escort party’s address, so drop the broken “on behalf” phrase entirely.","high","applied"],
    ["s0247","literal","they bow once more, advance slightly, and submit on behalf the words of those who escorted the empress;","they bow once more, advance slightly, and submit the words of those who escorted the empress;","Same ungrammatical “on behalf the words” in the literal field; the proposed “on their behalf” remains unnatural, so revise to the clear rendering of 附奏送後之詞 as submitting the escorts’ words.","high","applied"]
  ],
